  "architecturalPlan": {
    "constructionScope": "exterior",
    "scaleRationale": "The 242 m² single-storey enclosed envelope is sized to hold four bedrooms plus generous shared living capacity without treating the luxury brief or property value as a fixed area formula; exact room partitions remain deferred.",
    "levels": 1,
    "enclosedAreaM2": 242,
    "arrivalAndCirculation": "Arrival approaches the landward south-west face on a ground slab with a +0.20 m walking datum, passes under a supported 3.30 m-high entry canopy, and enters through the real rear threshold; all public, private, and service capacity is intentionally kept at this accessible level.",
    "volumeHierarchy": "A 22.0 × 11.0 m primary residence rises from floor top +0.20 m to 3.80 m eaves beneath a 1.40 m gable roof, while the lower 3.40 m terrace canopy and entry canopy form subordinate climatic thresholds.",
    "relationshipsAndViews": "The ocean-facing glazed façade opens directly onto a 5.75 m deep terrace at the same +0.20 m datum, which reaches the pool’s near dry deck without crossing water; the pool and broad view terrace sit beyond the living frontage while the sheltered arrival remains at the opposite façade.",
    "roofFacadeAndMaterials": "Warm ivory enclosure, limestone pool coping and terrace surfaces, bronze-framed glazing, and timber screens create a restrained Caribbean palette; the deep 0.80 m gable eaves shade the full residence, while low flat canopies and side screens deepen the arrival and outdoor-living façades.",
